# .repo-status -- the publish decision, where tooling can read it.
# Template: publish-status.example in repo-secret-scan. One of: never | not-yet | ready | public.

publish: not-yet
reason:  meant to be public so people can run the web customizer from GitHub Pages
review:  2026-10-14
blockers:
  - the owner's decision: making the repository public is his step (Q3)
# Reviewed 14 Oct 2026 (Q151): every stored file in history (1037 blobs) and every commit
# message (140 commits, all branches and tags) was searched for private IPs, email addresses,
# machine paths, private host names, MAC addresses and prices. The hits are the owner's noreply
# address, GitHub's bot address, test fixtures (example.com, home.arpa) and version numbers; no
# private detail. CI's secrets-history job scans the history for credentials on every pull
# request. The design and a model exist (v0.3.0); nothing is test printed yet, which the README
# says.
